\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Detailed Description\par
\pard\plain 
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
High-performance zero-copy networking interface. \par
}{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
The XLIO Ultra API is a performance-oriented, event-based networking interface designed for applications requiring maximum throughput and minimal latency. It provides zero-copy capabilities and efficient memory management for high-performance networking.\par
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAABX}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAABX}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Key Features
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Key Features}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Native zero-copy TX and RX operations\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Immediate callback-based event notification without accumulation\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Optimized data path with fewer corner cases and non-performance-oriented features{
\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
No blocking mode\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
No partial writes\par}
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Simplified application development:{
\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Fewer error conditions and corner cases to handle\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Flexible control of TX data aggregation\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
High-level TX operation completion\par}
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Concurrency and scalability:{
\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
No global namespace - sockets grouped by polling groups\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Clear concurrency boundaries and scalability model\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Each group can be handled independently by different threads\par}
}
\par
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAABY}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAABY}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Architecture Overview
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Architecture Overview}
The API is built around three main concepts:{
\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
1.\tab {\b Polling Groups} : Event management and callback registration\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
2.\tab {\b Sockets} : TCP socket abstraction with zero-copy capabilities\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
3.\tab {\b Buffers} : Memory management for zero-copy operations\par}
\par
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAABZ}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAABZ}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Typical Workflow
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Typical Workflow}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
1.\tab Initialize XLIO with {\field {\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK  \\l "AAAAAAAAAB" }{}}{\fldrslt {\cs37\ul\cf2 xlio_init_ex()}}}\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
2.\tab Create polling group with {\field {\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK  \\l "AAAAAAAAAF" }{}}{\fldrslt {\cs37\ul\cf2 xlio_poll_group_create()}}}\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
3.\tab Create socket with {\field {\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK  \\l "AAAAAAAAAL" }{}}{\fldrslt {\cs37\ul\cf2 xlio_socket_create()}}}\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
4.\tab Configure socket (bind, connect, listen)\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
5.\tab Poll for events with {\field {\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK  \\l "AAAAAAAAAK" }{}}{\fldrslt {\cs37\ul\cf2 xlio_poll_group_poll()}}}\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
6.\tab Handle events via registered callbacks\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
7.\tab Send/receive data using zero-copy operations\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
8.\tab Clean up resources\par}
\par
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAACA}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAACA}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Concurrency and Thread Safety
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Concurrency and Thread Safety}
The XLIO Ultra API is designed for high-performance applications with specific concurrency patterns and thread safety requirements.\par
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAACB}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAACB}
{{\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid 
Thread Safety Model
\par}
{\tc\tcl4 \v Thread Safety Model}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b The API is NOT thread-safe by default} \par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Applications are responsible for proper serialization when accessing XLIO objects from multiple threads\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
No internal locking is provided to maximize performance\par}
\par
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAACC}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAACC}
{{\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid 
Polling Group Concurrency
\par}
{\tc\tcl4 \v Polling Group Concurrency}
Polling groups are the primary mechanism for achieving concurrency:{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b Multiple polling groups can be polled concurrently}  from different threads\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b Polling groups do not share resources}  with each other\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b Sockets from different groups can be handled concurrently}  without serialization\par}
\par
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAACD}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAACD}
{{\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid 
Serialization Requirements
\par}
{\tc\tcl4 \v Serialization Requirements}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b Within a polling group} : All operations require serialization{
\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Only one thread should call {\field {\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK  \\l "AAAAAAAAAK" }{}}{\fldrslt {\cs37\ul\cf2 xlio_poll_group_poll()}}} per group at a time\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Socket operations within the same group must be serialized\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Serialized polling group and socket calls can be executed by different threads\par}
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b Across polling groups} : No serialization required{
\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Different threads can operate on different groups simultaneously\par}
}
\par
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAACE}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAACE}
{{\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid 
Thread Safety Exceptions
\par}
{\tc\tcl4 \v Thread Safety Exceptions}
Some operations have specific thread safety characteristics:{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b Initialization} : {\field {\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK  \\l "AAAAAAAAAB" }{}}{\fldrslt {\cs37\ul\cf2 xlio_init_ex()}}} and {\field {\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK  \\l "AAAAAAAAAE" }{}}{\fldrslt {\cs37\ul\cf2 xlio_exit()}}} are not thread-safe\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
A group created with the flag XLIO_GROUP_FLAG_SAFE can execute a polling and socket TX operations concurrently\par}
\par
\par}
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAACF}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAACF}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Current Limitations
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Current Limitations}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
TCP sockets only (no UDP support)\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
No crypto offload support\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
No bonding support\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Only busy polling is supported\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
fork() is supported only without created polling groups \par}
\par
\par}
