\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid 
Detailed Description\par
\pard\plain 
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Functions for managing polling groups and event handling. \par
}{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Polling groups are the core event management mechanism in the XLIO Ultra API. They allow applications to register event callbacks and efficiently poll for network events across multiple sockets.\par
Polling group is a collection of sockets and resources required for their operation. Different polling groups can be used concurrently without serialization.\par
Polling groups provide loggical sockets organization for the following purposes:{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Achieving concurrency and scaling\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Implementing different RX / completion logic\par}
\par
Recommendations:{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Groups are expected to be long lived objects. Frequent creation/destruction has a penalty.\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Reduce the number of different network interfaces within a group to minimum. This will optimize the HW objects utilization. However, maintaining extra groups can have an overhead. \par}
\par
}{\pard\widctlpar\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brsp20 \adjustright \par}
